\ spread ( coll -- v0 v1 ... vN-1 ) — push the elements of a collection
\ onto the data stack. For frames, pushes :key v :key v ... in key order.
\ Accepts array, set, and frame; errors on other types.

\ basic array spread
[ 10 20 30 ] spread .s clear cr          \ [ 10 20 30 ]

\ empty array — nothing pushed
[ ] spread .s clear cr                   \ [ ]

\ single-element array
[ 42 ] spread . cr                       \ 42

\ mixed types
[ "a" 5 :sym ] spread .s clear cr        \ [ a 5 :sym ]

\ nested values stay intact (each item pushed as-is)
[ [ 1 2 ] [ 3 4 ] ] spread .s clear cr   \ [ [ 1 2 ] [ 3 4 ] ]

\ set: elements come out in the set's internal (sorted) order
[< 3 1 2 >] spread .s clear cr             \ [ 1 2 3 ]

\ empty set
[< >] spread .s clear cr                   \ [ ]

\ frame: pushes :key value :key value ... in key-sort order
{ :a 1 :b 2 } spread .s clear cr         \ [ :a 1 :b 2 ]

\ frame: keys come back as symbols (not raw cells)
{ :x 10 } spread swap . . cr             \ :x 10

\ empty frame
{ } spread .s clear cr                   \ [ ]

\ round-trip: spread an array then rebuild
[ 1 2 3 ] spread 3 array . cr            \ [ 1 2 3 ]

\ non-collection — error
42 spread
"hello" spread
:sym spread

\ spread into a locals head names the pieces
: three-fields | a b c | c . b . a . cr ;
[ 1 2 3 ] spread three-fields                   \ 3 2 1

\ empty stack — underflow
spread
